1
00:00:09,013 --> 00:00:13,730
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:32,093
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

3
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:03,200
Qin Ming.

4
00:01:05,599 --> 00:01:06,920
Is this question really that hard?

5
00:01:37,239 --> 00:01:38,840
(Are you awake? Something happened.)

6
00:01:39,519 --> 00:01:40,439
We just closed a case last night.

7
00:01:40,439 --> 00:01:41,519
What happened this time?

8
00:01:41,599 --> 00:01:42,480
(It's serious.)

9
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:43,400
(The cats ate someone.)

10
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:50,100
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 1=

11
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:55,000
(Police)

12
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,760
Ms. Chen, what's going on?

13
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:01,959
Someone's dead.

14
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:02,959
How did she die?

15
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,319
The cats ate her.

16
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:07,760
(Do Not Enter; Police)

17
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,120
Qin, you're finally here.

18
00:02:10,159 --> 00:02:10,840
Any later,

19
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:12,319
and the rain would've ruined the scene.

20
00:02:12,639 --> 00:02:14,439
Isn't it your job to protect the scene?

21
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,240
Don't worry.

22
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,919
We kept the scene fully protected.

23
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:25,919
Dr. Qin,

24
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,680
don't you think
that cat's gaze is creepier

25
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,400
than a normal one's?

26
00:02:30,439 --> 00:02:32,120
Dilated pupils, trembling muscles.

27
00:02:32,199 --> 00:02:34,039
Focus on checking
for stimulants or hallucinogens.

28
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:43,920
(Forensic Autopsy - External)

29
00:02:49,479 --> 00:02:50,400
Most of the wounds on the body

30
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,439
are consistent
with cat bites and scratches.

31
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:54,000
But none of them were fatal.

32
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,159
The victim had multiple abrasions.

33
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,520
She likely sustained them

34
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,919
while struggling violently
inside this cage.

35
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,520
This cage...

36
00:03:03,599 --> 00:03:05,240
You don't need a cage
to feed stray cats.

37
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,159
This cage

38
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,960
was set here on purpose.

39
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,800
That's what I thought.

40
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,599
Why would you need
such a big cage for wild cats?

41
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:14,319
Remember to take the cat food back.

42
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,400
Let's check what these cats
were actually fed.

43
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,120
Got it.

44
00:03:17,319 --> 00:03:18,680
If you're right,

45
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:20,120
someone drugged the cats,

46
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:21,439
staged the scene,

47
00:03:21,439 --> 00:03:22,439
and more importantly,

48
00:03:22,479 --> 00:03:23,919
the door was locked from the inside.

49
00:03:24,159 --> 00:03:25,039
Then wouldn't that make this...?

50
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,400
A locked-room murder.

51
00:03:26,599 --> 00:03:27,919
Someone wanted her dead.

52
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,400
Shiyu,

53
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:30,840
that's Han Liang's job.

54
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:31,919
Qin,

55
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,039
let her speak her mind.

56
00:03:34,039 --> 00:03:35,120
We're a team.

57
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,280
The fatal wound is here.

58
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,479
It's spindle-shaped, with clean edges.

59
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,840
It was caused by a sharp weapon.

60
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,319
The blade pierced her heart.

61
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,560
She died from blood loss.

62
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,479
This sunflower

63
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,520
was deliberately placed here.

64
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,439
The killer left a letter.

65
00:03:59,719 --> 00:04:00,439
We've examined it.

66
00:04:00,439 --> 00:04:01,800
There are no fingerprints on it.

67
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,759
Where was it found?

68
00:04:02,759 --> 00:04:04,039
Under the victim's body.

69
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,280
The person in the cage

70
00:04:06,319 --> 00:04:07,520
is also the one who built it.

71
00:04:07,879 --> 00:04:09,000
She imprisoned souls,

72
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,400
only to be consumed by hunger.

73
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,400
Listen,

74
00:04:11,599 --> 00:04:12,840
the cats out there are hungry.

75
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,800
- They're licking an impure heart.
- Let me out!

76
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,240
This is the first judgment

77
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,680
and also a declaration.

78
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:18,920
Retribution has come.

79
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,879
Every sin will be paid for.

80
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:22,160
Retribution?

81
00:04:22,759 --> 00:04:24,079
What an arrogant claim.

82
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,000
It's a direct challenge to the police.

83
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,639
Only one set of tire tracks nearby.

84
00:04:30,639 --> 00:04:32,240
Long stop, deep tracks.

85
00:04:32,519 --> 00:04:33,639
The rain didn't wash them away.

86
00:04:33,639 --> 00:04:35,360
Looks like a sedan.

87
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,120
Barely any public transport around here.

88
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:38,600
Only private cars can get in.

89
00:04:38,759 --> 00:04:40,079
If there's only one set of tracks,

90
00:04:40,079 --> 00:04:41,800
the killer and the victim
must've arrived together.

91
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:43,920
This area is remote,
and the roads are winding.

92
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,560
There are hardly any cameras.

93
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,959
But a sedan was caught on camera
coming here

94
00:04:47,959 --> 00:04:48,720
three days ago.

95
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,519
But we never caught it leaving.

96
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,399
And the plate number?

97
00:04:51,439 --> 00:04:52,399
It isn't clear.

98
00:04:52,519 --> 00:04:53,680
Then run the vehicle records.

99
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:54,600
What else did you find?

100
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,240
The lock's got scratches on it.

101
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,920
(Double Safe)
Someone used a pro lock pick.

102
00:04:58,399 --> 00:05:00,399
The handle's got
scuff marks from a chain.

103
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,839
Probably more than one lock.

104
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,839
This keyhole was forged.

105
00:05:03,839 --> 00:05:04,879
(Double Safe)
It can be freely opened.

106
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,399
So this wasn't a locked room.

107
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,040
The female victim

108
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:09,560
was killed by a single stab wound.

109
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,680
It's most likely a homicide.

110
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,759
I heard she was attacked by cats.

111
00:05:12,759 --> 00:05:15,040
The forensic team says
it was caused by drugs.

112
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,240
Everyone, go back
and compile your findings.

113
00:05:17,319 --> 00:05:19,399
We'll meet in two hours.

114
00:05:19,399 --> 00:05:20,199
Yes, sir.

115
00:05:27,639 --> 00:05:29,120
The dust has fresh scuff marks.

116
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,439
Someone must've lain prone here,
observing.

117
00:05:42,399 --> 00:05:43,160
Qin,

118
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,600
we found this back there.

119
00:05:48,639 --> 00:05:50,319
She was a drug addict too?

120
00:05:51,279 --> 00:05:52,879
Let's head back and see

121
00:05:53,079 --> 00:05:54,519
what else the body's got to say.

122
00:05:56,279 --> 00:05:57,240
Let's do a second autopsy.

123
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,720
Focus on linking external wounds

124
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,959
to internal injuries.

125
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,399
The victim's stomach
was completely empty.

126
00:06:18,639 --> 00:06:19,879
There was no intestinal content.

127
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:21,319
Judging from her intestines,

128
00:06:21,319 --> 00:06:21,879
the victim

129
00:06:21,879 --> 00:06:23,399
hadn't eaten for at least 24 hours
before her death.

130
00:06:23,399 --> 00:06:25,800
She was imprisoned and starved too?

131
00:06:26,759 --> 00:06:27,600
After six hours without food,

132
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,680
the stomach can be completely empty.

133
00:06:30,319 --> 00:06:31,360
A single-edged stabbing weapon

134
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:34,040
entered upward at an angle,
from right to left,

135
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:35,160
piercing the pericardium directly

136
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,360
and causing cardiac tamponade.

137
00:06:36,639 --> 00:06:38,199
That's consistent
with the initial findings.

138
00:06:38,279 --> 00:06:39,600
This was indeed the fatal wound.

139
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:41,160
So that means

140
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:43,879
the feral cats were used
to destroy the body

141
00:06:43,879 --> 00:06:45,040
and conceal the truth.

142
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:47,399
More importantly,
look at the angle of force.

143
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:50,240
If the killer attacked from the front

144
00:06:50,519 --> 00:06:51,399
to create this kind of

145
00:06:51,399 --> 00:06:53,639
right-to-left penetrating wound

146
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,439
and hit a vital organ so precisely,

147
00:06:55,879 --> 00:06:57,040
the killer must be left-handed.

148
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,560
A lefty...

149
00:06:59,759 --> 00:07:01,720
That stab was brutal

150
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,399
and extremely calculated.

151
00:07:03,639 --> 00:07:05,399
Based on the crime scene,

152
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:06,759
it looks more like

153
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,759
it was all planned.

154
00:07:09,639 --> 00:07:10,560
(Don't kill me.)

155
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,360
(Don't kill me.)

156
00:07:17,173 --> 00:07:20,240
(Retribution has come.
Every sin will be paid for.)

157
00:07:22,439 --> 00:07:24,639
Based on the autopsy and this letter,

158
00:07:24,959 --> 00:07:26,240
we can confirm it was homicide.

159
00:07:26,879 --> 00:07:27,680
Han Liang,

160
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,360
have you identified the victim?

161
00:07:30,399 --> 00:07:31,360
The victim was Su Shi.

162
00:07:31,439 --> 00:07:32,519
She was a manager at Sun Group,

163
00:07:32,519 --> 00:07:33,759
Longfan's leading company.

164
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,160
She took leave two weeks ago.

165
00:07:35,199 --> 00:07:36,480
According to her staff,

166
00:07:36,519 --> 00:07:39,040
she was very sociable
and had many friends.

167
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:39,839
But this time,

168
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,399
no one knew where she went.

169
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:42,120
Li,

170
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:42,959
I've got some things

171
00:07:42,959 --> 00:07:44,079
to take care of.

172
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:45,360
I won't be in the office.

173
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:47,160
Keep an eye on things for me.

174
00:07:47,519 --> 00:07:48,439
Sure, Ms. Su.

175
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,199
Besides work,

176
00:07:52,199 --> 00:07:53,480
did Su Shi have any special hobbies

177
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,920
or particular social circles?

178
00:07:55,399 --> 00:07:57,680
She was good at using her advantages.

179
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:59,959
She'd pick pretty girls

180
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,839
from poor families
who were a little ambitious,

181
00:08:01,839 --> 00:08:02,759
and bring them into the game.

182
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:05,759
If a woman wants to climb the ladder,

183
00:08:06,839 --> 00:08:10,079
she must learn how to make men

184
00:08:10,959 --> 00:08:13,600
gladly pave the way for her.

185
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,160
Do you understand?

186
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:19,079
- Yes, Ms. Su.
- Yes, Ms. Su.

187
00:08:19,319 --> 00:08:20,120
Are you saying

188
00:08:20,279 --> 00:08:22,560
Su Shi was always teaching
those girls this?

189
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,240
Yes.

190
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,199
But strangely,

191
00:08:24,439 --> 00:08:26,279
she was very lenient with those girls,

192
00:08:26,279 --> 00:08:28,360
yet especially strict
with her own daughter.

193
00:08:33,759 --> 00:08:34,679
What were you doing just now?

194
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:35,840
Why were you talking to him?

195
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:36,960
I wasn't.

196
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:39,360
I was just saying hi to Uncle Le.

197
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,679
How many times have I told you

198
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:42,919
not to come here looking for me?

199
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,759
Didn't you hear me?

200
00:08:43,759 --> 00:08:44,799
Can't you remember?

201
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:46,759
You did it on purpose, huh?

202
00:08:47,679 --> 00:08:49,600
You deliberately talked to him, huh?

203
00:08:49,919 --> 00:08:51,639
No, I didn't.

204
00:08:51,919 --> 00:08:54,039
The school camp fee is due.

205
00:08:54,039 --> 00:08:55,240
I tried calling you,

206
00:08:55,879 --> 00:08:56,799
but I couldn't get through.

207
00:08:56,799 --> 00:08:58,159
I told you, you're not going!

208
00:08:58,159 --> 00:08:58,919
Why would you join

209
00:08:58,919 --> 00:08:59,919
some overnight trip

210
00:08:59,919 --> 00:09:01,159
with boys and girls mixed together?

211
00:09:01,639 --> 00:09:03,559
I know what's on your mind.

212
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,240
That Lu boy is going too, isn't he?

213
00:09:12,799 --> 00:09:13,879
Be a good girl.

214
00:09:14,519 --> 00:09:16,399
Stay away from those boys.

215
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,639
Also,

216
00:09:20,039 --> 00:09:22,000
don't come here again.

217
00:09:33,159 --> 00:09:34,480
It's all for your own good.

218
00:09:36,799 --> 00:09:38,039
I have a dinner engagement tonight.

219
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,960
Go home by yourself, okay?

220
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,759
I'll check the security cameras

221
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,799
to make sure you get home.

222
00:09:47,799 --> 00:09:48,759
Half an hour.

223
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:49,919
Is that enough?

224
00:09:54,879 --> 00:09:56,559
The victim's daughter, Su Tang,

225
00:09:56,679 --> 00:09:57,919
has a long history of drug use

226
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,399
and recently disappeared.

227
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:00,559
She can be listed as a suspect.

228
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:03,399
Based on the wounds on the body,

229
00:10:03,399 --> 00:10:04,759
the staged locked door,

230
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:07,120
and the use of the cats,

231
00:10:07,799 --> 00:10:09,360
the killer must've
known the victim well.

232
00:10:09,679 --> 00:10:11,279
Likely someone close to her.

233
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,120
My conclusion

234
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:13,679
supports Han Liang's theory.

235
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:19,039
Any clues from this letter?

236
00:10:19,039 --> 00:10:20,600
The killer is very good
at avoiding detection.

237
00:10:20,799 --> 00:10:22,000
They didn't leave much behind.

238
00:10:23,519 --> 00:10:25,240
From a psychological perspective,

239
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:27,080
the killer left the letter
at the crime scene

240
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:29,559
mainly to control the narrative
around the victim's death

241
00:10:29,559 --> 00:10:32,440
and declare the victim's crimes
in their own way.

242
00:10:32,919 --> 00:10:35,559
It's a ritual unique to the killer.

243
00:10:35,639 --> 00:10:37,960
We focused on Su Tang's call records

244
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,200
and found a suspicious number

245
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,080
that kept in regular touch with her.

246
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,559
Especially before the murder,

247
00:10:42,559 --> 00:10:44,000
the contacts suddenly spiked.

248
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:45,840
The number wasn't registered
under a real name.

249
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,200
It was a fake identity.

250
00:10:47,279 --> 00:10:48,960
But based on cell tower data,

251
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:49,879
we found

252
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,240
the number's activity

253
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,200
was centered around the Fengshan Villas.

254
00:10:58,066 --> 00:10:59,373
(Central Zone of Fengshan Villas)

255
00:10:59,799 --> 00:11:00,679
Find Su Tang

256
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:02,360
and we may find the answers.

257
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,000
Hi there,

258
00:11:48,879 --> 00:11:50,960
(Ten Years Ago)
how about moving around?

259
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,399
The photo'll come out more natural.

260
00:12:06,399 --> 00:12:07,639
You're pretty good at this.

261
00:12:07,639 --> 00:12:08,679
Take a couple for me too.

262
00:12:09,279 --> 00:12:11,279
Sorry, the light's gone.

263
00:12:11,559 --> 00:12:12,879
Xia Wen, I'll take them for you.

264
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:25,693
(Police)

265
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,120
Keke.

266
00:12:42,919 --> 00:12:43,759
Why?

267
00:12:45,039 --> 00:12:45,960
I dropped out of school.

268
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:47,559
Was it because of Xia Wen?

269
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,759
What exactly happened that day?

270
00:12:50,519 --> 00:12:52,080
I saw you two leave together.

271
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,080
That night,

272
00:12:58,720 --> 00:12:59,798
I kept waiting for you.

273
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,759
I never planned to go.

274
00:13:21,799 --> 00:13:24,039
(With growing environmental awareness,)

275
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,159
(our city has launched)

276
00:13:25,159 --> 00:13:27,039
(a large-scale tree-planting campaign.)

277
00:13:28,159 --> 00:13:29,440
(Residents are doing their part)

278
00:13:29,679 --> 00:13:31,519
(to make our city greener.)

279
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:33,879
Eat more. You've lost weight.

280
00:13:34,919 --> 00:13:36,120
You must be tired.

281
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,639
Mom,

282
00:13:38,279 --> 00:13:39,639
I took tomorrow off.

283
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:43,200
You don't have to.

284
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:45,000
I can go by myself.

285
00:13:46,159 --> 00:13:46,960
Mom,

286
00:13:47,759 --> 00:13:49,840
tomorrow is the tenth anniversary
of Wen's death.

287
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,200
I want to go.

288
00:13:52,679 --> 00:13:53,480
After all...

289
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,399
If Wen knew how well you treat me,

290
00:14:03,519 --> 00:14:05,360
she'd be so happy.

291
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:08,799
(Yesterday, a woman's body
was discovered)

292
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:10,159
(in the outskirts of Fengshan.)

293
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,480
(Police rushed)

294
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:13,960
(to secure and investigate the scene.)

295
00:14:14,039 --> 00:14:15,600
(Fengshan Outskirts Murder)
(After a preliminary examination,)

296
00:14:15,759 --> 00:14:16,799
(the incident was determined)

297
00:14:16,799 --> 00:14:18,519
(to be a serious criminal case.)

298
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,639
(The collection of evidence
at the scene)

299
00:14:20,639 --> 00:14:22,440
(and the investigation
of the surrounding area)

300
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,200
(are being carried out.)

301
00:14:23,559 --> 00:14:25,919
(Police seek witnesses)

302
00:14:25,919 --> 00:14:27,120
(and useful leads,)

303
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,759
(and promise confidentiality
for informants.)

304
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,279
(We'll follow the case)

305
00:14:31,279 --> 00:14:33,039
(and bring you the updates.)

306
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:37,400
♪Fingerprints seal the verdict♪
(Memorial Tablet for Xia Wen)

307
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:43,700
♪Good deeds bloom from lies♪

308
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:48,380
♪Who's next nailed to this wall?♪

309
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:56,266
♪The Executer is never late♪

310
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:01,586
♪Every sin will be paid for♪

311
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:30,200
♪The sunflower bows, reciting names♪

312
00:15:31,106 --> 00:15:34,880
♪Each petal is a solemn phrase♪

313
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:39,500
♪And moonlight, forever justly♪

314
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:42,906
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

315
00:15:46,426 --> 00:15:51,380
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

316
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:55,820
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

317
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:21,453
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

318
00:16:22,010 --> 00:16:26,160
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

319
00:16:26,333 --> 00:16:30,010
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

320
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:34,586
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

321
00:16:43,626 --> 00:16:47,300
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

322
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:50,020
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

323
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:54,760
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

324
00:16:54,826 --> 00:16:58,580
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

325
00:16:58,906 --> 00:17:03,180
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

326
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:07,560
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

327
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:11,840
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

328
00:17:12,613 --> 00:17:16,500
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

329
00:17:25,490 --> 00:17:29,280
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

330
00:17:29,693 --> 00:17:33,570
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

331
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:37,480
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

332
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:40,490
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

333
00:17:40,546 --> 00:17:45,210
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

334
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:49,600
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

335
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:52,370
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

336
00:17:52,426 --> 00:17:54,170
♪We stop here in this night♪

337
00:17:54,466 --> 00:17:58,860
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

338
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:04,653
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

339
00:18:07,506 --> 00:18:13,180
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

340
